  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine, a nasal decongestant, is shown to bind to Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6, both of which participate in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, which is ultimately linked to Cyp2c19. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Brompheniramine may influence Cyp2c19 through the modulation of its substrate metabolism. The shared involvement of Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6 in the same metabolic pathway, coupled with their participation in the same enzymatic activity, indicates a possible functional overlap in their roles. The final scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of arachidonic acid metabolism, which could have implications for the regulation of inflammatory responses and other physiological processes.",
